\end{equation}

where  $f_{\sigma,\eta}(1)=1$ (we use the notation $1$ to denote the identity element in $G$, and its projection to $Z$), after identifying $\bar{k}(Z)^{*} / \bar{k}^{*}$ with $\{f \in \bar{k}(Z)^{*}: f(1)=1\}\subset \bar{k}(Z)^*$.


Because of Lemma \ref{Lem:easier_calculation}, applied to $Z=G/(H^u\cdot Z_{H^{red}})$, and Lemma \ref{Lem:derived} we may assume without loss of generality (after changing $\beta$ by a coborder), that $D_{\sigma} \in \pi^*\Div^0(G^{ab}) + \alpha^*\Div(Y)$.

By definition of $\Div_{\overline{T_G}}(Z)$, we have that the following identities hold:

\begin{align}
