\end{align}

We will assume throughout the rest of the proof that all the specializations of functions at the specific points appearing are $\neq 0$. This may always be done without loss of generality.




We start the computation of the RHS of (\ref{Eq:2pairings}).

\begin{lemma}\label{Lem:RHS}
	The following identity holds:
	\begin{equation}\label{Eq:abelian}
