\label{Lem:SameImage}
	Let $C$ be a good complex. The groups $\P^0(K,C)$ and $(\P^0(K,C))^{\wedge}$ have same image in $\mathbb{H}^2(K,C^d)^D$, under the morphism $\theta:(\P^0(K,C))^{\wedge} \rightarrow \mathbb{H}^2(K,C^d)^D$ defined by local duality 
	(we recall that $\theta$ is the map induced from local duality as in (\ref{Mor:theta})).

The compactness of $\P^0(K,C)/\overline{\mathbb{H}^0(K,C)}$ implies that its image in  $\P^0(K,C)^{\wedge}/{\mathbb{H}^0(K,C)}^{\wedge}$ is closed. Since it is also, by the definition of profinite completion, dense, we see that its image is the whole quotient $\P^0(K,C)^{\wedge}/{\mathbb{H}^0(K,C)}^{\wedge}$.

The corollary now follows from the following commutative diagram:
\begin{center}
	\begin{tikzcd}
	\mathbb{H}^0(K,C) \arrow[hook,r] \arrow[d] &\P^0(K,C)\arrow[r,"\theta"] \arrow[d] &\mathbb{H}^2(K,C^d)^D \arrow[d,equal]\\
	(\mathbb{H}^0(K,C))^{\wedge} \arrow[r] &(\P^0(K,C))^{\wedge}\arrow[r,"\theta"] &\mathbb{H}^2(K,C^d)^D
	\end{tikzcd},
\end{center}

of which both rows are complexes and the second one is exact.

